{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Restore</b> — the poet speaks in the language of Israel." "<b>Like streams</b> — like strong waters." "<b>In the Negev</b> — it is always hot, because of the sun, or after the language of Targum: נגובו מיא (the waters were dried up)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 126, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:19.314353820Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}